# Z80_LoadDriver: it runs with interrupts masked, and the `move.w (a7)+,sr` that ends it lets the
# V-int that fell due meanwhile in before its rts, so every corpus call (one per run, at boot) took
# an interrupt and none was compared. This runs it untimed from its first call's entry state;
# Z80_BusRequest's poll of $A11100 reads 0 (the bus granted).
case boot
